# User Accounts UI — Task Plan & Implementation Log

## Plan
- High-level goal: Build the Accounts Management (User Accounts) UI under the ADMINISTRATION module strictly for the IQA role, matching the v1 layout reference with DaisyUI 5 components and modular frontend architecture.
- Scope:
  - Frontend only: `Index.vue`, `UserFilterBar.vue`, `UserTable.vue`, `PreRegisterModal.vue`.
  - Minimal web route and controller mapping so `/admin/users` is accessible in browser.
  - Sidebar and Topbar remain untouched (inherited from `AppShell`).
  - Purely scoped to IQA role persona.
- Key decisions:
  - Component library: 100% DaisyUI 5 (`btn`, `table table-pin-rows`, `badge badge-soft`, `tabs tabs-box`, `input`, `select`, `modal`).
  - Modularity (Ponytail): Keep every Vue SFC strictly under 150-200 lines by extracting partials.
  - Realistic initial state conforming to the reference screenshot: 13 institutional users, status pill tabs with counts, role filter, and action buttons.
- Edge cases to handle:
  - Empty search / filter results state with clear reset button.
  - Responsive table container with horizontal scroll protection.
  - Fallback initials when avatar photo is missing.

